 "check": {
  "describe": "A tap on 'Your ride is here' at 0.1 s, captured 0.15 s later. The row is about halfway off to the right and Battery has not moved yet (BEFORE); after the 350 ms exit, Battery moves up into the gap (Java, C++ and TS alike). Resized (narrow 240, wide 540) the rows fill the width, the Restore button stays at the right, and the dismissed row slides out by its own width. Mono looks have no motion: the tapped row is already gone and Battery has moved up.",
